      "type": "model",
      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I have all the information. Let me work through the problem carefully.\n\n**Setup:** A, B fixed; C at distance 2 from line AB; D at distance 1 from line AB; dihedral angle C−AB−D = 60°.\n\nLet me set coordinates. Take AB as the x-axis: A=(0,0,0), B=(b,0,0). The distance from C to AB is 2, so C=(x₁, 2cosθ, 2sinθ) — actually let me place C in a plane perpendicular to AB. Let C=(c, 2, 0) (distance 2 from x-axis), and D=(d, cos60°·1, sin60°·1) = (d, 1/2, √3/2) since the dihedral angle between plane ABC and plane ABD is 60°, and D is at distance 1.\n\n**Option A: ∠CAD ≥ 60°**\nVectors AC=(c,2,0), AD=(d, 1/2, √3/2). \nAC·AD = cd + 1. |AC|≥2, |AD|≥1.\ncos∠CAD = (cd+1)/(|AC||AD|). This can be made large (e.g., c=d large), so ∠CAD can be small. **A is false.**\n\n**Option B: CD ≥ √3**\nCD² = (c−d)² + (2−1/2)² + (0−√3/2)² = (c−d)² + 9/4 + 3/4 = (c−d)² + 3 ≥ 3.\nSo CD ≥ √3. **B is true.**\n\n**Option C: When AB⊥CD, is CD⊥plane ABD?**\nAB⊥CD means the x-component of CD is 0, i.e., c=d. Then CD = (0, 3/2, −√3/2). Plane ABD contains AB (x-axis) and AD=(d,1/2,√3/2). Normal of plane ABD = AB × AD = (1,0,0)×(d,1/2,√3/2) = (0, −√3/2, 1/2). CD·normal = 0 + (3/2)(−√3/2) + (−√3/2)(1/2) = −3√3/4 − √3/4 = −√3 ≠ 0. So CD is not parallel to the normal, hence not perpendicular to plane ABD. **C is false.**\n\n**Option D: When AB⊥plane ACD, is AC⊥AD?**\nAB⊥plane ACD means AB is perpendicular to both AC and AD. AB⊥AC means c=0; AB⊥AD means d=0. Then AC=(0,2,0), AD=(0,1/2,√3/2). AC·AD = 0 + 1 + 0 = 1 ≠ 0. So AC is not ⊥ AD. **D is false.**\n\nSo the answer is **B**.",
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "id": "call_ff5ad1a6e41b426d97acd047",
            "index": 0,
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "submit_solution",
              "arguments": "{\"region_id\": \"region_art_0018_01\", \"final_answer\": \"B（CD ≥ √3）\", \"reasoning\": \"建立坐标系：取直线AB为x轴，A=(0,0,0)，B=(b,0,0)。因C到AB距离为2，可设C=(c,2,0)；因D到AB距离为1且二面角C−AB−D=60°，可设D=(d,1/2,√3/2)（把D放在与平面ABC成60°的平面内，其在垂直AB截面内的分量长为1，方向与C的垂线方向夹角60°）。\\n\\n逐项判断：\\nA. AC=(c,2,0)，AD=(d,1/2,√3/2)，AC·AD=cd+1。当c、d都很大时cos∠CAD=(cd+1)/(|AC||AD|)可接近1，∠CAD可远小于60°，故A错误。\\nB. CD²=(c−d)²+(2−1/2)²+(0−√3/2)²=(c−d)²+9/4+3/4=(c−d)²+3≥3，所以CD≥√3，B正确。\\nC. AB⊥CD即CD的x分量为0，得c=d，此时CD=(0,3/2,−√3/2)。平面ABD的法向量为AB×AD=(1,0,0)×(d,1/2,√3/2)=(0,−√3/2,1/2)。CD·法向量=−3√3/4−√3/4=−√3≠0，故CD不垂直于平面ABD，C错误。\\nD. AB⊥平面ACD要求AB同时垂直于AC和AD，即c=0且d=0，此时AC=(0,2,0)，AD=(0,1/2,√3/2)，AC·AD=1≠0，故AC不垂直于AD，D错误。\\n\\n综上，正确选项为B。\"}"
